meta {
  name: 8. Sell Escrow (After 30-Second Window Expires)
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/escrows/{{escrowId}}/sell
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "requested_by": "acc_seller_001",
    "settlement_notes": "30-second return window elapsed. Releasing funds from vault to merchant/seller."
  }
}

docs {
  **Sell Escrow**: Releases vault funds to the Merchant/Seller.
  
  **Mandatory Rules**:
  1. Escrow Status MUST be `DELIVERED`. (Returns `HTTP 400 Bad Request` if in `CREATED`, `FUNDED`, `HELD`, or any other state).
  2. Delivery Time / 30-Second Return Window MUST be checked. If 60 seconds have not passed, returns `HTTP 400 Bad Request`.
  3. To release funds early during the 30-second return window, use `POST /api/v1/escrows/{id}/accept-early`.
}

